  clock: 3  # cd39
  nonce: cd39  # cd39
  message: "Closing as wont_do — the intent is already implemented via a structurally stronger mechanism than executing the per-row diagnostic_test.cmd would have been.\n\nThe regression guard 'producer added for a DEPRECATE-NO-FOLD value' is enforced by:\n- audit_findings.find_zero_producer_violations() at packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/audit_findings.py:420.\n- Live-tree CI test test_live_tree_deprecate_no_fold_has_zero_producers() at packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/test_audit_findings.py:1072.\n\nFor every DEPRECATE-NO-FOLD verdict across docs/audits/*.md, the test runs the producer-coherence AST walker (find_emitted_symbol_kinds / find_emitted_evidence_types / find_emitted_edge_types) and fails on any producer emit site. The walker covers more shapes than executing diagnostic_test.cmd would have:\n\n- Literal-kwarg form: both grep and walker.\n- Assignment-form to Name (kind = '…'; Symbol(kind=kind)): walker only — WI-nubuv ext A landed 2026-05-06.\n- F-string expansion (f'ast_{x}' with x resolvable to a literal set): walker only — WI-nubuv ext B landed in PR #3636 (2026-05-11).\n- Module-level constant resolution: walker only.\n\nThe walker docstring explicitly cites the Fundamental Concept Audit playbook §'Step 4.5 — Indirection-aware producer trace' — the same source as this WI's description (2026-05-07 lab notebook §'High-value #3').\n\nOf the 17 DEPRECATE-NO-FOLD rows currently in the audit docs, only 2 have git-grep-style diagnostic_test.cmd (both subsumed by the walker). The other 15 are python3 registry-membership asserts for CANONICAL/FOLD verdicts, which are unrelated to producer existence and are already enforced by the L1 drift linters (check-symbol-kind-drift / check-evidence-type-drift / check-edge-type-drift) and the registry property tests in test_symbol_kinds.py / test_evidence_types.py / test_edge_types.py.\n\nExecuting diagnostic_test.cmd would be redundant for the git-grep rows and weaker (no indirection coverage), and orthogonal to producer-existence for the python3 rows. The diagnostic_test field itself remains useful documentation — 'here's the test the audit author ran when filing this verdict' — but doesn't need machine execution at CI time."  # cd39
